---
import {
  Alert02Icon,
  Analytics01Icon,
  FileSearchIcon,
  Route01Icon,
} from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
import FeaturePage from '@/components/FeaturePage.astro'

const related = [
  { title: 'seo crawl', text: 'Crawl the site from your machine and list technical issues.', href: '/docs/crawl', icon: Route01Icon },
  { title: 'seo page', text: 'One URL: what it serves now, its index status and its queries.', href: '/docs/page', icon: FileSearchIcon },
  { title: 'seo index', text: 'Pages that lost their clicks, checked live and with URL Inspection.', href: '/docs/indexing', icon: Alert02Icon },
  { title: 'seo report', text: 'Search Console sections that show where to look first.', href: '/docs/report', icon: Analytics01Icon },
]
---

<FeaturePage
  title="SEO audit tool for AI agents"
  description="Run a website SEO audit with your AI agent: a technical site crawl, single page checks, pages that lost their clicks and the Search Console report."
  path="/features/seo-audit"
  lead="Find the pages that are broken, blocked or losing search traffic, and give your agent enough evidence to fix the cause."
  {related}
>
  <h2>What an audit covers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>What it checks</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><a href="/docs/crawl">seo crawl</a></td><td>Status codes, redirects, titles, descriptions, canonical and robots tags, and broken internal links across the site. Runs on your machine with the CLI.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/docs/page">seo page</a></td><td>One URL as it is served now, plus what Google URL Inspection reports for it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/docs/indexing">seo index</a></td><td>Pages that lost most of their clicks, checked live and with URL Inspection, so you see which ones broke or left the index.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/docs/report">seo report</a></td><td>Search Console sections such as content decay, cannibalization and traffic drops.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Start with a crawl, then follow the clicks</h2>
  <p>
    Run the crawl first to get a technical baseline, and save it so the next
    crawl can be compared after a release. Then use the index check and the
    report to see which issues line up with lost search traffic. A long list
    of warnings matters less than the few pages that stopped getting clicks.
  </p>

  <h2>Observations, not verdicts</h2>
  <p>
    A <code>noindex</code> tag or a canonical that points elsewhere is
    reported as what the page says. It is only a problem if you did not mean
    it. The audit gives your agent the evidence, and you decide what to fix.
  </p>
</FeaturePage>
